In article <1994Jan29.143213.15000@ned.cray.com>, rowanjj@topaz.cray.com (Jeff Rowan) writes...
>Jeffrey the Knight requests your assistance (trying to sound
>chivalrous ;):
> 
>I'm running 3.1.3 on my 386 PC and experienced some sort of
>glitch -- my screen froze and I had to reboot (sigh).  Not really
>sure what happened (gremlin in my CPU?)
> 
>After the reboot I saw all of my "level files" (JEFFREY_.xx)
>exist so I typed `recover jeffrey_' getting the following:
> 
>	c:/games/nethack/recover.exe: cannot chdir to
>	/usr/games/lib/nethackdir.
> 
>Aargh! I'm not using UNIX!!  Can someone tell me how to get the
>correct version of RECOVER.EXE so I gan get this game restarted.
>I would REALLY appreciate the help as this is the first time I've
>gotten a Knight past the Quest.

Don't care about the display of unix style path names. It will
work all the same. But you have to specify the actual path with 
the -d option.
For example: Make a backup copy of your jeffrey*.* files, then
change to your nethack directory. I think the PC386 version cannot
use a bones directiry :-(.
Then enter: RECOVER -d . JEFFREY_
This should work. Note that you have to enter the complete filename
up to the . but without the . and without the extension.
So, if your files were named jeff_9.*, you'd have to enter
RECOVER -d . JEFF_9

Hope this helps, and we'll here soon that your knight ascended.

(Minispoiler)
Btw.: On an MSDOS-PC, you can also use backup copies of your character's
.sav files


